From: "John M. Bozeman" <jmb5b@faraday.clas.virginia.edu>
Date: Mon, 28 Nov 1994 18:43:37 -0500 (EST)
Subject: [#94-11-473] GENE: Resurrecting the dodo?

In favor of bringing back the dodo:  it  is not only sort of cute,
   it has been demonstrated to be unable to compete with other
   species.  This is a Good Thing, in case they get away and
   try to colonize other ecosystems.  

Against:  I really think that the first thing that will be 
   "brought back" will be something like a lab mouse... we
   have to be able to clone an animal before we can start
   resurrecting extinct species!

On the other hand, I think it would be really interesting to 
   try to bring back the pteridactle (sp?).  We tend to think
   of them as being on the large side, but according to the
   exhibit the Albaquerque Museum of Natural History, most
   were fairly small (wing span of about a meter?).  They
   were supposedly quite agile, too... I would love to see
   one fly!  (Though a flying reptile would probably be
   VERY bad to release into an ecosystem!  Hmm... it might 
   take care of all those city pigeons, though...)

               John

