On Sun, 27 Nov 1994, Craig Presson wrote:

> My paranoid little 10-yr-old son just asked where on earth are the
> best and worst places in terms of natural disaster potential. Does
> anyone have suggestions for places, or sources of data?

I live in Vancouver and the current threat is earthquakes. I don't even
know when Vancouver had it's last major (or for that matter minor)
earthquake. I recall two small tremors over the past few years, but that's
about it. I don't think Vancouver has had a major (a la California)
earthquake this century.

This means that we'll likely get a major pressure release sometime. The
guesses by seismologists et al seem to put it within ten years. And
if you've ever seen the downtown core and the West End (which has one of
the high population densities on the continent if I remember my facts)
you'll notice the large number of residential buildings over 20 or 30
stories...

Of course, they're all supposed to earthquake safe, but...

Anyway, I'm always kind of edgy, mainly because I don't have all the
equipment currently that I'd like to have in the event I no longer
have a home when I come back from work...

